{0 Actions and sources}

A machine does not touch the page, the network or the clock. It asks its host.
There are two forms of request:

- An {e action} ({!Silica.Action.t}) is done once, at a step: focus an element,
  push a URL, copy a text.
- A {e source} belongs to a state. It starts when the machine enters the state
  and stops when the machine leaves it: a timer, a Remote call, a Live
  subscription, a key binding, a focus trap.

Because a source belongs to a state, it cannot run after its state is left.
The checker uses this rule: every running timer, call and subscription must
belong to the current state.

{1:actions Actions}

A step gives actions in [goto ~actions], [reenter ~actions] and [stay actions], and a
case gives them in [entry] and [exit]. [Copy_machine.make ?start] gives the
actions of the start.

{t
| Action | What the host does |
|---------|--------------------|
| [Focus ref], [Blur ref] | move keyboard focus to the element, or take it away |
| [Scroll_into_view ref] | scroll the element into view by the smallest distance |
| [Scroll_to] | scroll an element, or the window, to a position |
| [Measure] | read the size and position of an element, and raise an event with it |
| [Copy] | write a text to the clipboard; [on_result] gets [true] when it worked |
| [Load_script] | load a script once for each URL, and raise an event when it ran or failed |
| [Navigate url], [Replace url], [Back], [Forward], [Reload] | move in the history |
| [Resume nav], [Revert_navigation] | let a stopped navigation happen, or undo the last one (see {!page-router.block}) |
| [Preload request] | fetch a Remote call now, for a page that needs it soon |
| [Set_title] | set the document title |
| [Set_status] | the HTTP status of a server render |
| [Set_document_attribute] | set or remove an attribute of [<html>], such as [data-theme] |
| [Set_cookie] | store a cookie that the server can read |
| [Remount] | end the child components of this machine, so they start again |
}

An action with a result ([Measure], [Copy], [Load_script]) raises its event in
the instance that ran it, in any state. When that instance has ended, the
event is dropped.

This button copies a text and shows the result for two seconds. The [Shown]
state owns the timer, so the timer stops when the state is left:

{@mlx file=examples/shared/doc_copy.mlx[
open Silica

type event = Copy | Result of bool | Back

module States = struct
  type _ t = Ready : unit t | Shown : bool t
end

module Copy_machine = Machine.Make (States)

let text = "Hello from Silica"

let machine =
  Copy_machine.make ~id:"copy" ~init:(Copy_machine.at Ready ())
    [
      Copy_machine.state Ready "ready" ~to_:[ Shown ] (fun () -> function
        | Copy ->
            Copy_machine.stay
              [ Action.Copy { text; on_result = Some (fun ok -> Result ok) } ]
        | Result ok ->
            Copy_machine.goto Shown ok
        | Back ->
            Copy_machine.unhandled
        );
      Copy_machine.state Shown "shown" ~to_:[ Ready ]
        ~after:[ (2000, Back) ]
        (fun _ -> function
          | Back ->
              Copy_machine.goto Ready ()
          | Copy | Result _ ->
              Copy_machine.unhandled
          );
    ]

let view (snapshot : Copy_machine.snapshot) : event Node.t =
  match snapshot with
  | Copy_machine.At (Ready, ()) ->
      <div>
        <code>(Node.text text)</code>
        <button on_press=Copy>"Copy the text"</button>
      </div>
  | Copy_machine.At (Shown, true) ->
      <p>"Copied."</p>
  | Copy_machine.At (Shown, false) ->
      <p>"The browser did not allow the copy."</p>

let component = Component.make machine view
]}

The step gives the action to the host as [Run]:

{@ocaml[
# let snapshot, _ = Silica.Machine.start Doc_copy.machine;;
val snapshot : Doc_copy.Copy_machine.snapshot =
  Doc_copy.Copy_machine.At (Doc_copy.States.Ready, <poly>)
# let _, actions, _ = Silica.Machine.send Doc_copy.machine snapshot Doc_copy.Copy;;
val actions : Doc_copy.event Silica.Action.host list =
  [Silica.Action.Run
    (Silica.Action.Copy
      {Silica.Action.text = "Hello from Silica"; on_result = Some <fun>})]
]}

{1:sources Sources}

A state lists its sources in [invoke], and its timers in [after]:

{t
| Source | What it does while the state is active |
|--------|----------------------------------------|
| [after] | raise an event after a number of milliseconds |
| {!Silica.Source.call} | one Remote call; the answer is an event (see {!page-data.remote}) |
| {!Silica.Source.live} | follow one key of a topic (see {!page-data.topics}) |
| {!Silica.Source.keys} | a table of keys for the whole page; keys typed in a text field do not count, except with Ctrl or Meta, and Escape |
| {!Silica.Source.dismiss} | a dismiss layer: Escape, a press outside or focus that leaves raise events; the newest layer gets them first |
| {!Silica.Source.focus_trap} | keep focus inside an element, and give it back at the end |
| {!Silica.Source.scroll_lock} | the page does not scroll |
| {!Silica.Source.outside_press} | a press outside an element raises an event |
| {!Silica.Source.anchor} | keep a popup next to another element |
| {!Silica.Source.resize}, {!Silica.Source.intersection}, {!Silica.Source.scroll} | an element changes size, enters or leaves the viewport, or scrolls |
| {!Silica.Source.visibility}, {!Silica.Source.online}, {!Silica.Source.media} | the document is visible, the browser is online, a media query matches |
| {!Silica.Source.block} | stop every navigation and raise an event instead (see {!page-router.block}) |
}

The sources that give a value, such as [media] and [online], raise it once at
the start, so the machine knows the value when it enters the state.

A source that takes refs gets them when the case is made. A component that
can show more than once in a page gives each instance its own refs with
{!Silica.Source.map_refs}, for example from an id in its props.

{1:rate Rate limits}

{!Silica.Rate} limits how often an input reaches a machine. [Throttle ms]
lets the first value through and then the last value of each window.
[Debounce ms] waits for a pause and gives the last value. Rate limits go on
event attributes ([on_input_rate], see {!page-components.jsx}) and on the
sources [keys], [resize], [intersection] and [scroll]. A debounce that is part
of the behaviour, such as "search after the user stops", is better as a state
with an [after] timer (see {!page-machines.outcomes}): then the checker sees
it.
